{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.MaximalTorus","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.MaximalTorus","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Category.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.NatTrans","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Types.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Defs"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MaximalTorus.rank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MaximalTorus.rank","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus.lean#L63-L63","doc":"**Maximality**: the torus is maximal — its rank equals the rank\nof the gauge group. For SU(2): `rank T = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MaximalTorus.diagonal_action","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MaximalTorus.diagonal_action","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus.lean#L59-L59","doc":"**Diagonal action**: the torus acts diagonally on each weight\nspace of `V`.  Abstractly the restriction of `embed(t)` to `V` is a\ndiagonal matrix in the weight basis; encoded here as: the image of\nthe torus under `embed` is abelian (diagonal automorphisms commute). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MaximalTorus.embed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MaximalTorus.embed","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus.lean#L54-L54","doc":"The torus embeds into the gauge group: every torus element\nyields a natural isomorphism `ω ≅ ω`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MaximalTorus.torusGroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MaximalTorus.torusGroup","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus.lean#L51-L51","doc":"The torus carries a group structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MaximalTorus.torusType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MaximalTorus.torusType","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus.lean#L49-L49","doc":"The diagonal automorphism type (abstracting `T ≅ U(1)^r`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MaximalTorus.numWeights","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MaximalTorus.numWeights","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus.lean#L47-L47","doc":"The number of weight spaces of `V` under the torus action.\nFor SU(2): `numWeights = 2` (the ±1/2 weight spaces). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MaximalTorus.fibreFunctor_faithful","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MaximalTorus.fibreFunctor_faithful","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus.lean#L44-L44","doc":"**Faithfulness** of the fibre functor (inherited from QuantumUniverse). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MaximalTorus.fibreFunctor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MaximalTorus.fibreFunctor","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus.lean#L42-L42","doc":"The fibre functor `ω : C → Type w` (from the QOU). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MaximalTorus.V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MaximalTorus.V","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus.lean#L40-L40","doc":"The fundamental object `V` of categorical dimension 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MaximalTorus.hopfObj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MaximalTorus.hopfObj","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus.lean#L38-L38","doc":"The Frobenius–Hopf object `A` in `C` (from the QOU). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MaximalTorus.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MaximalTorus.mk","kind":"ctor","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus.lean#L35-L35","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MaximalTorus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MaximalTorus","kind":"structure","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus.lean#L25-L63","doc":"**Maximal torus and weight subcategory**.\n\nGiven a quantum observable universe `(C, A, ω)` with fundamental object\n`V`, the weight subcategory `⟨V⟩ ⊂ C` is the full subcategory whose\nobjects are direct sums of weight spaces of `V`.  The maximal torus is\n`T = Aut⊗(ω|_{⟨V⟩})`, the subgroup of `G = Aut⊗(ω)` consisting of\nnatural automorphisms acting diagonally on each weight space.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:maximal-torus}`\nRef: [lusztig1993] https://doi.org/10.1007/978-0-8176-4717-9 ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:maximal-torus","label":"def:maximal-torus","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}